[{"order":1,"type":"heading","text":"Pivoting Architecture under Changing Business Requirements"},{"order":2,"type":"subheading","text":"Introduction to Architectural Adaptability"},{"order":3,"type":"paragraph","text":"In modern software engineering, business requirements are rarely static. As markets shift and product goals evolve, software architecture must be capable of pivoting without requiring a complete rewrite. This tutorial explores strategies and patterns for maintaining high adaptability in enterprise systems."},{"order":4,"type":"subheading","text":"Core Principles of Adaptable Systems"},{"order":5,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Loose Coupling: Ensure services interact through well-defined APIs to minimize cascading changes."},{"order":6,"type":"bullet_point","text":"High Cohesion: Group related functionalities together so changes are localized to specific modules."},{"order":7,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Abstracted Interfaces: Depend on abstractions rather than concrete implementations to easily swap out components."},{"order":8,"type":"subheading","text":"Refactoring Monoliths for Flexibility"},{"order":9,"type":"paragraph","text":"When business requirements force a pivot, monolithic applications often suffer from tight coupling. Introducing the Strategy Pattern allows algorithms or behaviors to be selected at runtime, minimizing structural code modifications."},{"order":10,"type":"code","text":"public interface PaymentStrategy {
    void processPayment(double amount);
}

public class CreditCardPayment implements PaymentStrategy {
    public void processPayment(double amount) {
        System.out.println("Processing credit card payment of $" + amount);
    }
}

public class PaymentContext {
    private PaymentStrategy strategy;
    public PaymentContext(PaymentStrategy strategy) {
        this.strategy = strategy;
    }
    public void executePayment(double amount) {
        strategy.processPayment(amount);
    }
}"},{"order":11,"type":"subheading","text":"Conclusion"},{"order":12,"type":"paragraph","text":"Architectural adaptability is not an accident; it is the result of deliberate design choices. By prioritizing loose coupling, utilizing robust design patterns like the Strategy Pattern, and embracing modularity, engineering teams can pivot efficiently when business requirements change."}]
